# Each example builds a binary named after its own directory, beside its source,
# so `cd examples/<name> && corral run -- ponyc --debug` leaves it there. They
# are listed one by one rather than matched with a pattern, because the pattern
# that would catch them - everything in an example directory without a dot in
# its name - would also silently ignore a source file that has no extension.

examples/first-representation/first-representation
examples/in-process-pooler/in-process-pooler
examples/pooler-learning/pooler-learning
examples/pooler-training-value/pooler-training-value
examples/boosting-value/boosting-value
examples/sequence-training-value/sequence-training-value
examples/actor-pooler/actor-pooler
examples/scalar-encoder/scalar-encoder
examples/grid-cells/grid-cells
examples/document-similarity/document-similarity
